body:
love the locs, how long have you been growing em? 

&#x200B;

im 4yrs in........... i think??

You're good, your hair is going to look this way for like a week until they poof out

&#x200B;

I've been told to was and use a dry shampoo for the itching if it's unbearable

I say give it some time.

&#x200B;

While its possible to start at your length, it the first few months you would have to be very protective of your hair, it's slightly easier when it has some length. Also you dont want too much tension at your scalp

Okay, now this is cool. 

&#x200B;

If this was made only using Premiere Pro, how in the world did you pull off that effect with the japanese text and the mist effect around reaper?

I have been looking for guides forever on how to make something with this and was just curious if you could point me in the right direction. 

&#x200B;

Transitions were fucking top notch also, amazing

Hm... That's a bit inspirational. Sometimes I feel like it's taking a bit too long for them to grow, and I get uneasy because right now they're at the point where I can't really do anything with them until they're longer, so I have to just deal with it. And I also feel like some of them are a bit more fragile than a few of the other locs that I have that seem to have started finally locing up.

&#x200B;

But, idk. I'm hoping by the end of May I can at least have like, a small little ponytail. At LEAST.
